function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    print("<div class=\"doc-detail-layout\"><main class=\"content doc-page doc-detail\"><div class=\"doc-title\"><h2>sqlite_info</h2><span class=\"call-boundary host-call\">host call</span></div><div class=\"doc-section signatures\"><h3>Capy</h3><pre>function sqlite_info(handle : u64, key : string) dval</pre></div><div class=\"doc-section content\"><h3>Description</h3><p><code>sqlite_info()</code> reads the latest error text, the last inserted row ID, or the changed-row count.</p><p>Each result is a <code>dval</code> with its natural value type. Use a converter only when an operation needs a static type.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section params\"><h3>Parameters</h3><div><p>handle : the SQLite connection handle</p></div><div><p>key : <code>error</code>, <code>insert_id</code>, or <code>affected_rows</code></p></div><div></div></div><div class=\"doc-section\"><h3>Return Values</h3><p>The value for <code>key</code>.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section\"><h3>Errors</h3><p>The function stops with an error for an unknown key. The error lists the valid keys.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">var db := sqlite_connect(&quot;:memory:&quot;)\nsqlite_query(db, &quot;create table t(id integer primary key)&quot;)\nsqlite_query(db, &quot;insert into t values(1)&quot;)\nvar message := sqlite_info(db, &quot;error&quot;)\nvar id := sqlite_info(db, &quot;insert_id&quot;)\nvar rows := sqlite_info(db, &quot;affected_rows&quot;)\nprint(message, &quot; &quot;, id, &quot; &quot;, rows, &quot;\\n&quot;)\nsqlite_disconnect(db)\n</pre></div></div></main><aside class=\"doc-section see-also\"><h3>See also</h3><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/sqlite-connect/\">sqlite_connect</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/sqlite-query/\">sqlite")
    print("_query</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/sqlite-disconnect/\">sqlite_disconnect</a></aside></div>")
}
